# Git workflow — push directly to `main`

**Default for all agents on this project:** commit and push **directly to `main`**. Do not open feature branches or pull requests unless the user explicitly asks.

## Required flow

1. `git checkout main && git pull origin main`
2. Make changes on `main`
3. `git add` → `git commit -m "..."` → `git push origin main`

## Do not (unless user explicitly requests)

- Create `cursor/*` feature branches
- Open draft or ready PRs as the default delivery path
- Leave work only on a branch without pushing to `main`

## When the user asks for a PR or branch

- Use a branch only for that task
- Still merge to `main` when done unless they want an open PR for review

## Commit messages

- Complete sentences; prefix by area (`feat(finn):`, `fix(nav):`, `docs:`)
- Push after each logical unit of work — do not accumulate unpushed commits

## Conflicts / sync

- Always pull `main` before starting work
- If push is rejected: `git pull --rebase origin main`, resolve, push again

